 ```
 
+`-a` opens CPU-wide events (`pid == -1`), which `kernel.perf_event_paranoid > 0`
+blocks even when per-process hardware events succeed. If it fails with a
+"perf_event_paranoid" hint, either drop `-a` and profile the workload directly, or
+lower the setting to `0`.
+
 Reuse existing `perf.data` instead of re-recording whenever the user prefers or the workload is hard to reproduce.
 
